                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>"Facial&nbsp;Plastic and Aesthetic&nbsp;Surgery" is an undergraduate course that integrates specialized disciplines with plastic surgery.It introduces not only the techniques and fundamental principles of plastic surgery but also incorporates extensive knowledge of specialty diseases. The curriculum focuses on functional restoration and aesthetic reconstruction of face organ. Topics include the historical development of “specialty-specific plastic surgery,” fundamental procedures and techniques, as well as the aesthetic characteristics, functions, and reconstructive techniques for the eyes, ears, nose, and face.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
